# --- sources: the registry is committed, the material is not (TEMPLATE_GUIDE.md §4) -
# `make fetch-source` extracts an arXiv tarball into papers/source/<id>/: third-party LaTeX,
# figures and sometimes data. Whether to commit someone else's PDF or source tree is the PI's
# call, never the template's, so neither is committed by default. papers/sources.yaml keeps
# every source identifiable and re-fetchable either way.
papers/**/*.pdf
papers/**/*.djvu
papers/source/
# Files copied out of the PI's Zotero/Calibre libraries by `scripts/library.py import`, plus
# a metadata.json each (full tags, collections, abstract). Someone else's papers and the PI's
# own organisation: neither is the template's to publish. The registry and refs.bib, which ARE
# committed, carry the identifiers and provenance.
papers/imported/
!papers/sources.yaml

# --- session transcripts live OUTSIDE the repository entirely -----------------------
# .claude/hooks/capture_session.py writes to $RESEARCH_RECORDS_DIR (default
# ~/.claude-research-records), never here: a transcript is near-verbatim and holds
# half-formed reasoning, and a repository's sharing permissions cannot be subtracted from a
# subfolder. handoff.md is the artifact meant to be read by other people, and it IS committed.

# --- drop folders: transient, README only is tracked -------------------------------
papers/_drop/*
!papers/_drop/README.md
code/_drop/*
!code/_drop/README.md

# --- automatic prompt captures -----------------------------------------------------
# The raw per-session log and the auto-captured long prompts are machine-written.
# Committing them is a project decision: uncomment to keep them out of history.
# docs/prompts/log/
# docs/prompts/auto/

# --- Julia -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Manifest.toml IS committed: it pins the exact environment behind every result.
*.jl.cov
*.jl.*.cov
*.jl.mem

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# uv.lock IS committed, for the same reason as Julia's Manifest.toml; src/python/.venv is not.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.egg-info/

# --- Mathematica -------------------------------------------------------------------
*.mx
*.nb~
*.nb.bak
*.wxf
*.wdx

# --- Claude Code: personal/local only ----------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/agent-memory-local/

# --- large or transient numerical output -------------------------------------------
data/raw/
data/tmp/
*.h5
*.jld2
*.npz
# Tool output from scripts/run: keep the folder and its README, never the log files.
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep
!logs/README.md

# --- generated documents (source .md stays tracked) --------------------------------
reports/*.pdf
reports/*.tex
reports/*.aux
reports/*.log
reports/*.out
reports/*.toc
reports/*.fls
reports/*.fdb_latexmk
reports/*.xdv
reports/*.synctex.gz
reports/*.meta.json
reports/*.meta.err
# Vector copies of the example figures. Their bytes change on each run (TeX font subsets get
# random names), so they are generated. The PNGs are tracked, because GitHub shows only those.
docs/figures/*.pdf

# --- editors / OS ------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
